## Technical Architecture

### System Overview

The centralized logging stack implements a three-tier architecture:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        AWS EC2 (t3.micro)                       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                 │
│  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐         │
│  │    Nginx     │  │  System      │  │   Other      │         │
│  │    Logs      │  │   Logs       │  │   Services   │         │
│  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘         │
│         │                 │                 │                   │
│         └─────────────────┼─────────────────┘                   │
│                           │                                      │
│                    ┌──────▼──────────┐                          │
│                    │   Promtail      │                          │
│                    │  (Collector)    │                          │
│                    │  Ports: 9080    │                          │
│                    │  Ports: 9095    │                          │
│                    └──────┬──────────┘                          │
│                           │ (ships logs)                        │
│         ┌─────────────────▼──────────────────┐                 │
│         │        Loki (3100)                 │                 │
│         │   - Stores logs in BoltDB          │                 │
│         │   - Indexes by labels              │                 │
│         │   - /var/lib/loki                  │                 │
│         └─────────────────┬──────────────────┘                 │
│                           │ (queries)                          │
│         ┌─────────────────▼──────────────────┐                 │
│         │      Grafana (3000)                │                 │
│         │   - Web UI for log search          │                 │
│         │   - Pre-configured Loki datasource │                 │
│         │   - admin/admin                    │                 │
│         └────────────────────────────────────┘                 │
│                                                                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Component Architecture

| Component | Purpose | Port(s) | Details |
|-----------|---------|---------|---------|
| **Loki** | Log storage and indexing | 3100 (push)<br>9096 (metrics) | Receives raw log streams, stores in BoltDB, indexes by labels |
| **Promtail** | Log collector | 9080 (metrics)<br>9095 (ready) | Tails log files, scrapes system logs, ships to Loki |
| **Grafana** | Log search & visualization | 3000 (HTTP) | Web UI, pre-configured Loki datasource, admin/admin |
| **Prometheus** | Metrics collection | 9090 | Scrapes node/service metrics |
| **Node Exporter** | System metrics | 9100 | Exports CPU, memory, disk metrics |

### Data Flow

```
1. Nginx writes request logs → /var/log/nginx/access.log & error.log
2. System writes event logs → /var/log/syslog
3. Promtail tails all log files and forwards to Loki (port 3100)
4. Loki indexes by labels (job, service, etc.) and stores in /var/lib/loki
5. Grafana queries Loki and renders search results in the browser
```

### Infrastructure as Code

All components are provisioned via **Terraform modules** and installed through **user_data.sh automation**. The monitoring setup scripts:

- Download binaries from GitHub (avoiding large artifacts in the repo)
- Configure systemd services for auto-start
- Ensure all prerequisites (directories, user accounts, permissions) are in place
- Run in background with nohup to avoid blocking EC2 initialization

