## How to Deploy

### Prerequisites

- Terraform installed locally
- AWS credentials configured (`~/.aws/credentials`)
- SSH key created for EC2 access
- Route 53 hosted zone for domain

### Quick Deploy

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/mosesekerin/hng-infrastructure.git
cd hng-infrastructure

# Copy example variables
cp environments/prod/example.tfvars environments/prod/terraform.tfvars

# Edit with your values
nano environments/prod/terraform.tfvars

# Plan the infrastructure
cd environments/prod
terraform plan

# Deploy
terraform apply -auto-approve

# Get outputs
terraform output

# Verify services
ssh -i ~/.ssh/hng-infrastructure.pem ubuntu@<instance-ip>

# Check service status
systemctl status loki
systemctl status promtail
systemctl status grafana

# Access Grafana
# Browser: http://<instance-ip>:3000
# Username: admin
# Password: admin
```

### Accessing the Services

| Service | URL | Credentials |
|---------|-----|-------------|
| **Grafana** | http://[IP]:3000 | admin / admin |
| **Prometheus** | http://[IP]:9090 | (no auth) |
| **Loki (API)** | http://[IP]:3100 | (no auth) |

### Expected Startup Sequence

```
1. EC2 instance launches
2. user_data.sh runs (takes ~2-3 minutes)
3. Nginx starts automatically
4. Prometheus & Node Exporter start
5. monitoring-setup.sh runs in background
   ├── Loki starts (~30 seconds)
   ├── Promtail starts (~20 seconds)
   ├── Grafana starts (~40 seconds, needs datasource setup)
   └── Auto-provisioning configures Loki datasource in Grafana
6. All services running, accessible on ports
7. Promtail begins shipping logs to Loki
8. Grafana ready for log search
```

Total time from `terraform apply` to fully operational: **~5 minutes**

### Troubleshooting

#### Service won't start

Check systemd status:
```bash
systemctl status loki
journalctl -u loki -n 50
```

Check file permissions:
```bash
ls -la /var/lib/loki/
ls -la /etc/loki/
```

#### Grafana can't connect to Loki

Verify Loki is running:
```bash
curl http://localhost:3100/ready
```

Check Grafana datasource:
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/api/datasources | jq '.[] | {name, url}'
```

#### Promtail not collecting logs

Verify permissions:
```bash
sudo -u promtail cat /var/log/nginx/error.log
sudo -u promtail cat /var/log/syslog
```

Check Promtail config:
```bash
cat /etc/promtail/promtail-config.yml
```

Verify positions file:
```bash
ls -la /var/lib/promtail/positions.yaml
```

